    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "When should I use this skill?",
        "answer": "Use it when an error appears deep in execution and the original bad input is unclear."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it run commands automatically?",
        "answer": "The skill provides command examples and a helper script. Users should approve and review commands before running them."
      },
      {
        "question": "What projects fit best?",
        "answer": "It fits codebases with stack traces, tests, and layered calls where data changes across boundaries."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it find test pollution?",
        "answer": "Yes. The included helper can run matched npm tests and stop when unwanted state appears."
      },
